ood my blood my sweat my tears  everything into it my time my energy to  get some dollars out and once that  starts to happen i expand and maybe you  need money for expansion but i hate  going into debt especially when you're  first starting up i strongly advise  against it because it can sink not only  your business but your entire personal  financial future you make one wrong  business decision and you're stuck  paying this loan off for the next 20  years i know it's hard starting the  business and i know  one of the biggest challenges is getting  money to do it as much as possible try  to start a service try not to spend  money until you find a way to make money  you test your concept out on a really  small scale show that it works before  you invest your own dollars and  especially somebody else's dollars into  the into the business  if you're going to talk to a bank again  the banks are probably the least  friendliest to startups of any kind of  investor  they want to see the three years of  traction history revenue growth with  your company  and if they don't have it they're going  to take a personal guarantee and  whatever money you want to take out  that's life dealing with the banks  i hope you enjoyed for those of you  watching you liked the video please give  it a thumbs up below and i'd love to  hear from you i love seeing the comments  come in they make my morning every day  please leave a comment below and if you  have a question i'll do a video response  for you if you leave a comment  underneath thank you guys i'll see you  soon
 

